726</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9297688-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9297688</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOGAWA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOGAWA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOGAWA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOGAWA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An information processing system includes a variable-speed processor, and as the processor speed increases, performance improves and power consumption increases. The system comprises scheduling means that decides which task to be processed at each time and passes control to the task according to the decision; power management means operated at regular intervals to predict the processor power consumption and determine the operating frequency; and means operated in response to a request from scheduling module to evaluate how the task fulfilled the request. The processor speed can be reduced as long as the fulfillment is agreeable, thus saving power.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un système de traitement de l'information comprenant un processeur à vitesse variable dont les performances et la consommation d'énergie augmentent avec la vitesse. Le système comprend: des moyens de distribution qui décident au coup par coup de la tâche à traiter et exécutent celle-ci en conséquence; des moyens de gestion de l'énergie intervenant à intervalles réguliers pour prédire la consommation d'énergie du processeur et déterminer la fréquence opérationnelle; et des moyens mis en oeuvre en réponse à une demande provenant d'un module de distribution pour évaluer les modalités d'exécution de la tâche en fonction de la demande. La vitesse du processeur peut être diminuée tant que les modalités d'exécution de la tâche restent agréables, ce qui permet d'économiser l'énergie.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>